{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"[2026-08-12T23:22:57Z] AWS alarm sweep ADDENDUM — follow-up firing pair triaged (read-only ops investigation)\n(migrated from childsafe-bizarre-lorikeet comment 13 — session-scoped ops/analysis record; original comment retained there, see the index comment on that ticket)\n\nADDENDUM — follow-up firing pair triaged, 2026-08-12T23:07Z (read-only throughout).\n\nFIRINGS (4) and (5).\n  rebar-gerrit-voter-errors            ALARM 23:07:07Z -> OK 23:13:07Z, datapoint 23:06Z Sum=1\n  rebar-review-bot-merge-change-errors ALARM 23:07:18Z -> OK 23:13:18Z, datapoint 23:06Z Sum=1\n\nBOTH ARE FALSE POSITIVES. No voter error and no merge-change error occurred. Both counts trace to a\nSINGLE journal line at 2026-08-12T23:02:26Z (CONTAINER_NAME=compose-review-bot-1) which is the\nreview-bot's own LLM code-review analysis prose, verbatim:\n\n    ...mits matching markers for every target (VOTER_ERROR, MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR, AUTODEPLOY_ERROR,\n    AUTODEPLOY_DEFERRED, gerrit_to_platform error, both interrupt reasons) and REPL_LOG is\n    populated. The rolled-up review_interrupts per_interval=2 arithmetic is consistent\n    (total 14 seeded, next run +2)\n\nNothing redacted; the line contains no secret. The reviewer was reviewing a change to\ninfra/scripts/observability.sh ITSELF — the cold-start seeding fix for widespread-zealous-narwhal\nfiled earlier in this same sweep — so it enumerated the marker vocabulary as prose, and the probe\ncounted that prose as two errors.\n\nMECHANISM. observability.sh sections 4 and 4c count markers with an UNANCHORED grep over the\nreview-bot container journal (grep -cE 'VOTER_ERROR' / 'MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR'). The review-bot writes\nits LLM output to that same stream, so the probe cannot distinguish its own alarm vocabulary from an\nactual error.\n\nPROOF IT IS NOT A REAL MARKER (full-journal counts; real markers are line-start under -o cat):\n  VOTER_ERROR        line-start real: 221   substring-anywhere: 222   offset file: 222\n  MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR line-start real:   0   substring-anywhere:   1   offset file:   1\nExactly one of the 222 voter counts is the false match. The merge-change counter has NEVER recorded\na real error in the entire retained journal — its ONLY count in history is this false positive, and\nthat is what fired its alarm.\n\nCOORDINATOR HYPOTHESIS REFUTED. The proposed cause (a patchset superseding a mid-review change 409ing\nthe bot's vote or merge call, amid the 1684-1688 push/review activity) does not hold: there is no\n409, no conflict and no Gerrit 4xx/5xx of any kind in 22:45-23:20Z. The trigger was textual, not a\nGerrit interaction.\n\nRECOVERY / STATE. Nothing was left in a bad state and nothing needed retrying, because nothing\nfailed. The review-bot voted normally before, during and after the alarm window — voter_voted at\n23:05:08Z, 23:13:04Z, 23:19:38Z. The counters 'self-cleared' only because the offset absorbed the\none-time count; that is arithmetic, not recovery. Side effect: the offset files are now permanently\ninflated by the false count (voter offset 222 vs 221 real markers).\n\nCLASSIFICATION: NEW DEFECT, and the alarms are NOT at fault — both are correct to fire on a nonzero\ncount; the count was fabricated. Do not tune either alarm. Filed as colossal-slothful-grouse\n(8c2f-8377-5044-4650), open/unclaimed, file impact infra/scripts/observability.sh.\n\nRELATION TO widespread-zealous-narwhal: same false-positive FAMILY (probe publishes counts for\nnon-events) but a DISTINCT mechanism — narwhal is an absent-offset cold start, grouse is an\nover-broad pattern matching the token as data. Both in observability.sh.\n\nRECURRENCE RISK IS ACTIVE AND SELF-REFERENTIAL. The trigger is any review that discusses\nobservability.sh or the marker vocabulary, and the fleet is landing observability.sh changes right\nnow (the narwhal fix is in review — its review text is literally what fired this). Expect these two\nalarms to re-fire on each further review of that file until grouse is fixed.\n\nRUNNING TALLY for this sweep: 5 firings since the 04:00Z baseline — 3 true-positive bound-exceeded\nreview interrupts (no tuning warranted) and 2 false positives from probe-side defects; 2 new bugs\nfiled (widespread-zealous-narwhal, colossal-slothful-grouse), both in infra/scripts/observability.sh.\n"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786588674386551001,"uuid":"d30b4023-6b4d-4874-b99b-ff6b3da5d021"}